cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "arifOS: Constitutional AI Kernel and AGI Substrate"
message: "If you use arifOS in research, please cite it as follows."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Fazil"
    given-names: "Muhammad Arif"
abstract: >
  arifOS is a constitutional governance kernel for AI agents, implemented as a
  Model Context Protocol (MCP) server. It enforces 13 constitutional floors
  (F1–F13) before any tool call, code mutation, or capital decision, returning
  auditable verdicts (SEAL, HOLD, SABAR, VOID). The kernel separates judgment
  from execution: the agent that acts cannot certify its own action (Gödel Lock).
  Irreversible decisions are recorded in an append-only, Merkle-anchored ledger
  (VAULT999).
keywords:
